 adverse drug events in a highly computerized hospital</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>165</volume><fpage>1111</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15911723</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MZN015C35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chaudhry</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Systematic review: impact of health information technology on quality, efficiency, and costs of medical care</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>144</volume><fpage>742</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16702590</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="MZN015C36"><citation citation-type="web"><collab>Institute for Safe Medication Practices</collab><source>ISMP's List of High-Alert Medications</source><access-date>(10 July 2007, date last accessed</access-date><comment><uri xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="http://www.ismp.org/Tools/highalertmedications.pdf">http://www.ismp.org/Tools/highalertmedications.pdf</uri></comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>